'''Playable characters''' in [[Kyoutou Project]] fell into two categories: '''Shikigami''' (式神, "Familiar Spirits") were animal-like familiars who could be mass-produced, while '''Shintou''' or '''Shintoutsukai''' (神刀使い, "Divine Sword Masters") were anime-style human characters who would appear as chibi versions of themselves during battle, generally costing more to deploy than Shikigami. Allies were sorted into four rarities: EX, Rare, Super Rare and Uber Rare.

Every Shintou unit had two names: one for the character and one for their weapon. The weapon would change depending on their variant. For example, the default [[Kyosaka Nanaho (Legend Rare Cat)|Kyosaka Nanaho]] unit held the title of Kyosaka Nanaho: Honoka (the name of her sword) while her squirtgun-wielding summer variant was called Kyosaka Nanaho: 77HO Splash.

